Package: mica-gce-agent
Version: 0.0.1-1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794096000
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mica build <mica@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Mica OS agent for SSH logins on Google Compute Engine
 Follows the instance's and the project's ssh-keys metadata, which gcloud
 compute ssh and the console's SSH button write: keeps a login account
 (mica-accounts' login class, group mica-gce-admins), a home on DATA and a key
 file in /run/mica/gce/keys for each user they name, and removes a user's keys
 when they leave the metadata or expire. Honours block-project-ssh-keys and
 enable-oslogin. Carries a systemd unit and an OpenRC script and enables
 neither: a Compute Engine product enables it.
